    "title": "Flash Flood Warning by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 156 AM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 4 inches of rain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1 to 3 inches in 30 minutes. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is likely ongoing. Slow storm motion and training could lead to isolated storm total rains as high as 7 inches. HAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing flash flooding. SOURCE...Radar. IMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban areas, highways, streets and underpasses. Some locations that will experience flash flooding include... San Antonio, Austin, New Braunfels, Schertz, Cibolo, Converse, Universal City, Live Oak, Selma, Dripping Springs, Wimberley, Canyon Lake Dam, Randolph AFB, San Antonio Int Airport, Canyon Lake, Alamo Heights, Windcrest, Terrell Hills, Bulverde and Garden Ridge. As of 1:40 AM CDT, the river gauge on North Gatlin Creek near Dripping Springs reported 3.91 inches of rain in less than 2 hours.",
